language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ added_corners: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Enter the digits 1 through 8 into the eight positions around the edge of a 3 by 3 grid whose centre is empty, using each digit exactly once. The corners are circles (C) and the middles of the sides are squares (F):
$
$   C F C
$   F   F
$   C F C
$
$ The number in each square must equal the sum of the numbers in the two circles adjoining it.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/added_corners.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ positions[k]: the digit in position k, numbered 1 to 8 in reading order (left to right, top to bottom): 1 top-left circle, 2 top square, 3 top-right circle, 4 left square, 5 right square, 6 bottom-left circle, 7 bottom square, 8 bottom-right circle
find positions : matrix indexed by [int(1..8)] of int(1..8)

such that
$ the digits 1 through 8 are each used exactly once
allDiff(positions),
$ the top square is the sum of the two top circles
positions[2] = positions[1] + positions[3],
$ the left square is the sum of the two left circles
positions[4] = positions[1] + positions[6],
$ the right square is the sum of the two right circles
positions[5] = positions[3] + positions[8],
$ the bottom square is the sum of the two bottom circles
positions[7] = positions[6] + positions[8]
